From 6ae67d99f16e7b732cfbac5015e1165a51154508 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teemu Haila <teemu.haila@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:54:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 23/36] drm/amd/display: drive the iMac20,x second tile in
 plain DP panel mode (A3)

The lean core drives every Apple second tile in eDP panel mode (alternate
scrambler reset, DPCD 0x10A bit 0), except the iMac Pro panel, which never
locks video that way. The iMac20,x panel (APP AE31/AE32) has never been
brought up in eDP panel mode. The one configuration known to light both
of its tiles, the t2linux 7003 patch on 2026-10-10, left link 1 in default
DP panel mode. Match that known-good state.

This is the cheapest thing to flip if the right tile trains but stays dark
(SINK_STATUS 0x205 = 00).

[adapter: new, Sysadmin patches/amdgpu-imac20-2-5k-stitch DESIGN.md A3]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SUvgXxxT5Apr7YLjKZVd2T
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
index daefc1129..5ff58613d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
@@ -2967,6 +2967,13 @@ static inline bool dc_link_is_apple_tiled_dp_panel_mode(const struct dc_link *li
 	switch (sink->edid_caps.product_id) {
 	case 0xAE1D:
 	case 0xAE1E:
+	/*
+	 * iMac20,x: untested in eDP panel mode. Plain DP mode is what the
+	 * t2linux iMac20 patch uses, and its second tile locked video that
+	 * way. If D1 shows the tile trained but dark (0x205 = 00), drop these.
+	 */
+	case 0xAE31:
+	case 0xAE32:
 		return true;
 	default:
 		return false;
-- 
